WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.067 --> 00:00:03.144
(bouncy, playful music)
(wheels spinning)

00:00:03.144 --> 00:00:04.444
- [Commentator] In Saskatoon, Saskatchewan

00:00:04.444 --> 00:00:08.052
you'll find four senior
citizens making socks.

00:00:08.052 --> 00:00:09.969
Lots and lots of socks.

00:00:11.326 --> 00:00:15.493
- [Bob] Socks by Bob have
knitted 11,662 as of today.

00:00:18.919 --> 00:00:20.881
- [Commentator] That's
pairs of socks (popping),

00:00:20.881 --> 00:00:22.094
which means Socks by Bob

00:00:22.094 --> 00:00:25.094
has knitted 23,324 individual socks,

00:00:27.015 --> 00:00:29.221
8.8 miles of socks,

00:00:29.221 --> 00:00:31.116
and they're all for charity.

00:00:31.116 --> 00:00:32.902
The man responsible for all these socks

00:00:32.902 --> 00:00:35.735
is none other than Bob Rutherford.

00:00:39.229 --> 00:00:41.067
Enter Bob's knitting machines.

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:42.774
These super-powered knitting machines

00:00:42.774 --> 00:00:45.200
go at 90 turns per second.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.605
That's pretty fast.

00:00:46.605 --> 00:00:48.788
But, what makes these machines special

00:00:48.788 --> 00:00:51.029
are that they're self-made.

00:00:51.029 --> 00:00:52.317
- I'm an experimenter.

00:00:52.317 --> 00:00:54.094
I just build things.

00:00:54.094 --> 00:00:58.540
And it took a long time to
figure out how to do it.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.617
But when you're retired and nothing to do,

00:01:01.617 --> 00:01:03.200
it just sorta grew.

00:01:06.215 --> 00:01:07.828
- [Commentator] Socks by Bob began in 2010

00:01:07.828 --> 00:01:10.475
after the passing of Bob's wife Edith.

00:01:10.475 --> 00:01:14.411
- I was a caregiver to
my wife before she died

00:01:14.411 --> 00:01:16.722
and my son came home and said,

00:01:16.722 --> 00:01:18.858
"Dad you need something to do."

00:01:18.858 --> 00:01:21.273
I said, "Well I've made these socks

00:01:21.273 --> 00:01:23.432
"on this first knitting machine."

00:01:23.432 --> 00:01:24.767
- [Commentator] And that sparked an idea,

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:27.310
making socks for those in need.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:28.842
But Bob doesn't work alone.

00:01:28.842 --> 00:01:31.037
He has plenty of help.

00:01:31.037 --> 00:01:33.788
- George cuts the tube length.

00:01:33.788 --> 00:01:38.160
Glynn and Barney, they rub-knit
tube socks by the roll.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:38.993
- [Commentator] Each week

00:01:38.993 --> 00:01:41.225
Bob and his team knit hundreds of socks

00:01:41.225 --> 00:01:43.779
that they then deliver to
countless homeless shelters

00:01:43.779 --> 00:01:45.091
all throughout Canada.

00:01:45.091 --> 00:01:49.549
- The socks are delivered in
Alberta, Saskatchewan, BC,

00:01:49.549 --> 00:01:51.175
in Red Deer, Calgary.

00:01:51.175 --> 00:01:54.936
Some of have gone to the
northern part of the province.

00:01:54.936 --> 00:01:57.994
In short, they go to where they're needed.

00:01:57.994 --> 00:01:59.534
(bouncy music)

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:02.273
People gotta keep involved.

00:02:02.273 --> 00:02:05.826
You just can't give up
because of bereavement

00:02:05.826 --> 00:02:07.742
or whatever the case may be.

00:02:07.742 --> 00:02:12.444
I think that knitting socks
for needy people is important.

00:02:12.444 --> 00:02:14.615
People have to reach out
and touch each other,

00:02:14.615 --> 00:02:16.565
I think, as they grow older,

00:02:16.565 --> 00:02:19.148
and this has helped me do that.

00:02:20.839 --> 00:02:24.241
And I think that's the key to life.

00:02:24.241 --> 00:02:25.564
You don't give up.

00:02:25.564 --> 00:02:27.085
And find a purpose.

00:02:27.085 --> 00:02:30.510
Find something that needs to be done

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:31.343
and do it.

00:02:37.986 --> 00:02:40.153
(binging)

